\paragraph{Schema complexity in dialogue and IE.}
\looseness=-1
The Schema-Guided Dialogue dataset~\citep{rastogi2020towards} and SGD-X~\citep{lee2022sgd} document degradation with schema linguistic variation; \citet{li2023evaluating} observe count-dependent degradation in ChatGPT IE. The relationship between label similarity and confusion has precedent in visual recognition \citep{dubey-2018-pairwise-confusion}, correlated label noise \citep{collier-2021-correlated-noise}, hierarchical classification \citep{deng-2010-imagenet}, and label confusion matrices \citep{guo-2021-label-confusion,muller2019when,peterson2019human}.

\paragraph{SCS novelty.}
\looseness=-1
SCS inherits the embedding-similarity criterion from LLM-PEE \citep{llm-pee-2025}. The metric is a means; the empirical findings are the contribution, enabled by a controlled experimental methodology that previous work lacked---BCS-controlled batches that isolate confusability from count. The use of embedding distance for type discrimination has parallels in metric learning \citep{snell2017prototypical} and zero-shot classification \citep{yin-2019-zero-shot-bench}. The modest pairwise $r^2$ (1.3--1.7\%) compounds at the ecological batch level to explain ${\sim}$22\% of cross-batch RE variance on FewRel (\S\ref{sec:bcs_controlled}).

\paragraph{Cross-model validation.}
\looseness=-1
The effect replicates on Meta-Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct: extreme-BCS gaps of $-$27.1\,pp (count 8) and $-$23.9\,pp (count 16), reaching 77--87\% of Qwen3-32B's gap (Table~\ref{tab:cross_model_bcs}). All three open-weight families (Qwen3-32B, LLaMA-70B, LLaMA-8B) show consistent negative BCS slopes on FewRel RE. Gemini 2.5 Flash provides partial but fragile corroboration ($\Delta = -17.6$\,pp at count 8) with substantial leverage sensitivity (leave-one-out Pearson: $r = -0.80 \to -0.42$, $p = 0.22$; Spearman: $\rho = -0.40 \to -0.18$, $p = 0.64$; Appendix~\ref{sec:appendix_cross_model_gemini}). LLaMA-8B and LLaMA-70B both show no NER BCS signal ($r{=}{-}0.13$, $p{=}0.36$ for 70B), confirming the task asymmetry across three models (Table~\ref{tab:cross_model_ner_null}).

